# A narrow heater on a slab over a heat sink: the surface temperature is P / (pi k) ln coth(pi x / (4 d)), and far away it decays as exp(-pi x / (2 d)).
# Reference: that closed form, within 3% (6% at the farthest probe) for a heater two cells wide.
title Line heater on a 2 um slab of conductivity 1.38
grid dx=0.125 dy=0.125
window width=32 ymin=-2 ymax=0
heater h xmin=-0.125 xmax=0.125 ymin=-0.125 ymax=0 power=0.1
probe p0 x=1.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p1 x=2.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p2 x=4.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p3 x=6.0625 y=-0.0625
expect response p0 h 214.29328 1e-7
expect response p1 h 92.4847514 1e-7
expect response p2 h 19.0021741 1e-7
expect response p3 h 3.95290287 1e-7
expect peak 77.1684184 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 4096
expect response p0 h 214.483 0.03
expect response p1 h 92.526 0.03
expect response p2 h 18.9912 0.03
expect response p3 h 3.94574 0.06
expect crosstalk p3 p2 h 0.20788 0.05
